# Flutter mobile rules

- Laravel `origin/staging` `docs/api/v1/openapi.yaml` is the API source of truth.
- Keep code feature-first, testable, and understandable without generic clean
  architecture boilerplate.
- Use Riverpod and go_router without code generation.
- Keep one configured Dio client. Never log auth request/response data.
- Keep bearer tokens only in the `TokenStorage` secure-storage abstraction.
- Never persist username/password, authenticator/recovery codes, or 2FA
  challenges.
- Clear local auth on authoritative rejection, not on timeout/offline/5xx.
- Put all user-facing strings in ARB files and maintain Arabic/English parity.
- Preserve Android namespace and application ID `tr.indirimgo.app`.
- Main/release Android must deny cleartext; only debug may allow local HTTP.
- Flutter must never calculate trusted prices or mutate financial state
  independently of Laravel.
